{"key":"568bb8f45bbba04c","source_file":"Potts Re.json","source_id":45872,"source_url":"concordance-resist-ppl-reniti","term":"Resist","headwords":["Resist","Resistance"],"latin":["Reniti","Contraniti","Renisus","Renitentia"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Resist"],"latin":["Reniti","Contraniti"]},{"english":["Resistance"],"latin":["Renisus","Renitentia"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","HH","SE","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"5558","subsection":null},"text":"They observe whether it Hows in without any spiritual resistance. For if the thing is not so a resistance from within is perceived. If no resistance is perceived by them, they suppose that it is so.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6559","subsection":"end"},"text":"(That they are good) is perceived from their resistance (to what is evil).","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"7342","subsection":null},"text":"Resistance from the will, and thence obstinacy. Signified, Explained.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"7342","subsection":"2"},"text":"If a man has the affection of self and the world... he cannot resist it, for this would be to resist his own life...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"8216","subsection":null},"text":"Resistance and impotence. Signified.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"83","subsection":null},"text":"See Resist. HH 479:2.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"479","subsection":null},"text":"When an Angel leaves his like there is constantly some resistance.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"6","subsection":"3"},"text":"The heavenly aura resists. TCR 173:3.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"61","subsection":null},"text":"Under Repugnance, see this reference.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"1696","subsection":null},"text":"He was subjected to motion (with resistance)...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"3927","subsection":null},"text":"By infusing a resistance...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"4194","subsection":null},"text":"They are driven to speak... with perception and thus resistance, or without much resistance...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"5972","subsection":null},"text":"The preacher feels a resistance, so that he can scarcely say those things, and this with variety according to the resistance. Explained.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"973","subsection":"end"},"text":"Occurs.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"resist-568bb8","url":"/meta/potts/resist-568bb8/"}